       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release.\n- **Single dose:** 1,700 mg is also well above the typical maximum single dose of about 1,000 mg. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nI suspect a typo. Possible intended doses include:\n- 850 mg three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg twice daily with meals\n- 1,700 mg total per day, split into divided doses\n\nPlease tell me the intended dose and frequency, or confirm that you really want 1,700 mg three times daily. If you do confirm, tell me the clinical rationale so I can add it to the order note. I'll enter the order once I have that."
      }
