       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review. 5,100 mg/day is double the labeled maximum, and I don't know of any recognized protocol that supports it. The risk is serious, mainly lactic acidosis, and it grows with a dose this high.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range now.** For example, 850 mg three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or another dose you choose. You can then titrate under the protocol.\n- **Use your hospital's override pathway.** If the protocol is real, the pharmacy or the prescriber's own order-entry process can enter it directly with the protocol referenced. That route has proper verification and documentation.\n- **Tell me if the dose was a typo.** I'll enter the corrected order right away.\n\nTell me which you'd like, and I'll enter the order."
